# Code of Conduct

## Our commitment

{{SITE_NAME}} is a community project. We want it to be a place where
people of any background feel comfortable filing an issue, asking a
question, or submitting their first pull request. Everyone interacting
with this project — in issues, pull requests, discussions, chat, or in
person at related events — is expected to help keep it that way.

## Expected behavior

- Be respectful of differing viewpoints, experience levels, and
  communication styles.
- Give and accept constructive feedback gracefully — critique the work,
  not the person.
- Assume good faith. Most confusion is a documentation gap, not bad
  intent.
- Be patient with newcomers. Everyone was new to this project once.

## Unacceptable behavior

- Harassment, insults, or personal attacks, public or private.
- Discriminatory jokes, language, or imagery.
- Publishing others' private information without consent.
- Sustained disruption of discussions, issues, or events.
- Any conduct that would reasonably be considered inappropriate in a
  professional or community setting.

## Scope

This applies within all project spaces (repository, issue tracker,
discussions, chat) and in public spaces when someone is representing the
project or its community.

## Reporting

If you experience or witness unacceptable behavior, report it to
{{MAINTAINER_CONTACT}}. Reports will be handled with discretion. We will
respond as promptly as we can and will not share the reporter's identity
without consent.

## Enforcement

Maintainers are responsible for clarifying and enforcing these standards
and may take any action they deem appropriate in response to violations —
from a warning to a temporary or permanent ban from project spaces.

